{"key":"nlp-basics-u1-01","seriesId":"nlp-basics","episode":"u1-01","title":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","fps":30,"duration":203.087,"durationInFrames":6093,"video":{"width":1920,"height":1080,"burnCaptions":true,"brand":"learnvi.in"},"badge":["UNIT 1 · LESSON 1","STAGES OF NLP"],"series":{"title":"NLP, Simply Explained","subtitle":"University NLP, one idea at a time, no heavy maths","runningPrompt":"","stops":[{"id":"u1-01","number":1,"name":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","stamp":"THE STAGES OF NLP: FROM LETTERS TO MEANING","topic":""},{"id":"u1-02","number":2,"name":"Tokenization: How Text Becomes Pieces","stamp":"TOKENIZATION: HOW TEXT BECOMES PIECES","topic":""},{"id":"u1-03","number":3,"name":"Text Classification: Teaching Computers to Sort Text","stamp":"TEXT CLASSIFICATION: TEACHING COMPUTERS TO SORT TEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u2-01","number":4,"name":"Morphology: The Building Blocks Inside Words","stamp":"MORPHOLOGY: THE BUILDING BLOCKS INSIDE WORDS","topic":""},{"id":"u2-02","number":5,"name":"Part-of-Speech Tagging: Is It a Noun or a Verb?","stamp":"PART-OF-SPEECH TAGGING: IS IT A NOUN OR A VERB?","topic":""},{"id":"u4-01","number":6,"name":"Word Vectors: Giving Words a Place on a Map","stamp":"WORD VECTORS: GIVING WORDS A PLACE ON A MAP","topic":""}]},"stop":{"number":1,"name":"The Stages of NLP: From Letters to Meaning","stamp":"THE STAGES OF NLP: FROM LETTERS TO MEANING"},"shorts":{"width":1080,"height":1920,"maxSeconds":60,"cta":"Full lesson: NLP, Simply Explained · Unit 1"},"thumbnail":{"headline":"How computers read a sentence","big":"5 stages"},"segments":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","component":"TitleCard","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c01","start":0.6,"end":7.268,"marks":{},"text":"Welcome to NLP, Simply Explained. This is unit 1, lesson 1: the stages of NLP.","words":[{"w":"Welcome","start":0.6},{"w":"to","start":1.053},{"w":"NLP,","start":1.507},{"w":"Simply","start":1.96},{"w":"Explained.","start":2.6},{"w":"This","start":3.36},{"w":"is","start":3.64},{"w":"unit","start":3.88},{"w":"1,","start":4.28},{"w":"lesson","start":4.68},{"w":"1:","start":5.08},{"w":"the","start":5.4},{"w":"stages","start":5.64},{"w":"of","start":6.183},{"w":"NLP.","start":6.725}]},{"id":"c02","start":7.668,"end":14.749,"marks":{},"text":"When you read a sentence, you understand it in a blink. A computer can't. It has to work its way up, one stage at a time.","words":[{"w":"When","start":7.668},{"w":"you","start":7.788},{"w":"read","start":7.908},{"w":"a","start":8.148},{"w":"sentence,","start":8.308},{"w":"you","start":8.828},{"w":"understand","start":9.028},{"w":"it","start":9.588},{"w":"in","start":9.748},{"w":"a","start":9.908},{"w":"blink.","start":9.988},{"w":"A","start":10.508},{"w":"computer","start":10.708},{"w":"can't.","start":11.308},{"w":"It","start":11.828},{"w":"has","start":12.068},{"w":"to","start":12.268},{"w":"work","start":12.468},{"w":"its","start":12.708},{"w":"way","start":12.948},{"w":"up,","start":13.148},{"w":"one","start":13.428},{"w":"stage","start":13.668},{"w":"at","start":14.068},{"w":"a","start":14.228},{"w":"time.","start":14.388}]}],"title":"Welcome","shortTitle":"Welcome","props":{"kicker":"Unit 1 · Lesson 1","title":"The Stages of NLP","subtitle":"How a computer climbs from letters to meaning"},"start":0.6,"end":14.749,"startFrame":0,"durationInFrames":470},{"id":"idea","kind":"core","component":"BigIdea","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c03","start":15.667,"end":22.654,"marks":{},"text":"Here is the one idea to remember from this lesson. Understanding a sentence is not one step. It is a staircase.","words":[{"w":"Here","start":15.667},{"w":"is","start":15.907},{"w":"the","start":16.107},{"w":"one","start":16.227},{"w":"idea","start":16.507},{"w":"to","start":16.987},{"w":"remember","start":17.147},{"w":"from","start":17.627},{"w":"this","start":17.96},{"w":"lesson.","start":18.294},{"w":"Understanding","start":18.627},{"w":"a","start":19.507},{"w":"sentence","start":19.667},{"w":"is","start":20.187},{"w":"not","start":20.387},{"w":"one","start":20.627},{"w":"step.","start":20.907},{"w":"It","start":21.387},{"w":"is","start":21.587},{"w":"a","start":21.747},{"w":"staircase.","start":21.907}]}],"title":"The big idea","shortTitle":"The big idea","props":{"kicker":"Key idea","text":"Understanding a sentence is not one step. It is a staircase.","highlight":["staircase"]},"start":15.667,"end":22.654,"startFrame":470,"durationInFrames":237},{"id":"stages","kind":"core","component":"Steps","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c04","start":23.567,"end":27.76,"marks":{},"text":"Let's climb it. There are five steps, and each one builds on the step below.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":23.567},{"w":"climb","start":23.887},{"w":"it.","start":24.287},{"w":"There","start":24.527},{"w":"are","start":24.727},{"w":"five","start":24.927},{"w":"steps,","start":25.247},{"w":"and","start":25.727},{"w":"each","start":25.927},{"w":"one","start":26.167},{"w":"builds","start":26.367},{"w":"on","start":26.727},{"w":"the","start":26.847},{"w":"step","start":26.967},{"w":"below.","start":27.327}]},{"id":"c05","start":28.16,"end":36.539,"marks":{},"text":"Step one is lexical analysis. The computer splits the text into words and tokens, and works out where sentences begin and end.","words":[{"w":"Step","start":28.16},{"w":"one","start":28.56},{"w":"is","start":28.88},{"w":"lexical","start":29.12},{"w":"analysis.","start":29.68},{"w":"The","start":30.6},{"w":"computer","start":30.88},{"w":"splits","start":31.4},{"w":"the","start":31.84},{"w":"text","start":31.96},{"w":"into","start":32.32},{"w":"words","start":32.6},{"w":"and","start":33},{"w":"tokens,","start":33.2},{"w":"and","start":33.84},{"w":"works","start":34.08},{"w":"out","start":34.44},{"w":"where","start":34.64},{"w":"sentences","start":34.84},{"w":"begin","start":35.52},{"w":"and","start":35.86},{"w":"end.","start":36.2}]},{"id":"c06","start":36.939,"end":44.941,"marks":{},"text":"Step two is morphological analysis. It looks inside each word for its parts. \"Barking\" is \"bark\" plus \"i n g\".","words":[{"w":"Step","start":36.939},{"w":"two","start":37.259},{"w":"is","start":37.579},{"w":"morphological","start":37.779},{"w":"analysis.","start":38.619},{"w":"It","start":39.499},{"w":"looks","start":39.739},{"w":"inside","start":40.059},{"w":"each","start":40.539},{"w":"word","start":40.819},{"w":"for","start":41.059},{"w":"its","start":41.219},{"w":"parts.","start":41.499},{"w":"\"Barking\"","start":42.179},{"w":"is","start":42.859},{"w":"\"bark\"","start":43.139},{"w":"plus","start":43.579},{"w":"\"i","start":44.019},{"w":"n","start":44.399},{"w":"g\".","start":44.779}]},{"id":"c07","start":45.341,"end":53.17,"marks":{},"text":"Step three is syntactic analysis. It works out the structure of the sentence: who is doing what, and which words belong together.","words":[{"w":"Step","start":45.341},{"w":"three","start":45.741},{"w":"is","start":46.021},{"w":"syntactic","start":46.221},{"w":"analysis.","start":46.901},{"w":"It","start":47.821},{"w":"works","start":48.061},{"w":"out","start":48.421},{"w":"the","start":48.581},{"w":"structure","start":48.701},{"w":"of","start":49.181},{"w":"the","start":49.301},{"w":"sentence:","start":49.461},{"w":"who","start":50.221},{"w":"is","start":50.421},{"w":"doing","start":50.661},{"w":"what,","start":51.101},{"w":"and","start":51.341},{"w":"which","start":51.581},{"w":"words","start":51.861},{"w":"belong","start":52.221},{"w":"together.","start":52.621}]},{"id":"c08","start":53.57,"end":59.237,"marks":{},"text":"Step four is semantic analysis. It works out the literal meaning of the words and the sentence.","words":[{"w":"Step","start":53.57},{"w":"four","start":53.89},{"w":"is","start":54.21},{"w":"semantic","start":54.41},{"w":"analysis.","start":54.97},{"w":"It","start":55.89},{"w":"works","start":56.17},{"w":"out","start":56.49},{"w":"the","start":56.65},{"w":"literal","start":56.77},{"w":"meaning","start":57.25},{"w":"of","start":57.57},{"w":"the","start":57.69},{"w":"words","start":57.85},{"w":"and","start":58.25},{"w":"the","start":58.41},{"w":"sentence.","start":58.61}]},{"id":"c09","start":59.637,"end":67.501,"marks":{},"text":"And step five is pragmatic analysis: what the speaker actually means in this situation, which can go beyond the literal words.","words":[{"w":"And","start":59.637},{"w":"step","start":59.797},{"w":"five","start":60.157},{"w":"is","start":60.517},{"w":"pragmatic","start":60.717},{"w":"analysis:","start":61.397},{"w":"what","start":62.357},{"w":"the","start":62.597},{"w":"speaker","start":62.837},{"w":"actually","start":63.357},{"w":"means","start":63.877},{"w":"in","start":64.197},{"w":"this","start":64.357},{"w":"situation,","start":64.557},{"w":"which","start":65.397},{"w":"can","start":65.637},{"w":"go","start":65.877},{"w":"beyond","start":66.117},{"w":"the","start":66.477},{"w":"literal","start":66.637},{"w":"words.","start":67.077}]}],"title":"The five stages","shortTitle":"The 5 stages every NLP system climbs","props":{"kicker":"The staircase","title":"Five stages, from letters to intent","steps":[{"label":"Lexical","detail":"words and tokens"},{"label":"Morphological","detail":"parts inside words"},{"label":"Syntactic","detail":"sentence structure"},{"label":"Semantic","detail":"literal meaning"},{"label":"Pragmatic","detail":"meaning in context"}]},"start":23.567,"end":67.501,"startFrame":707,"durationInFrames":1346},{"id":"walk","kind":"core","component":"Table","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c10","start":68.433,"end":75.171,"marks":{},"text":"Let's send one sentence up the staircase: \"The dogs were barking loudly\". The table shows what each stage finds.","words":[{"w":"Let's","start":68.553},{"w":"send","start":68.673},{"w":"one","start":69.033},{"w":"sentence","start":69.233},{"w":"up","start":69.753},{"w":"the","start":69.873},{"w":"staircase:","start":70.033},{"w":"\"The","start":70.713},{"w":"dogs","start":70.993},{"w":"were","start":71.393},{"w":"barking","start":71.593},{"w":"loudly\".","start":72.073},{"w":"The","start":72.753},{"w":"table","start":72.953},{"w":"shows","start":73.353},{"w":"what","start":73.753},{"w":"each","start":73.953},{"w":"stage","start":74.193},{"w":"finds.","start":74.593}]},{"id":"c11","start":75.571,"end":80.291,"marks":{},"text":"The lexical stage finds five words: the, dogs, were, barking, loudly.","words":[{"w":"The","start":75.571},{"w":"lexical","start":75.691},{"w":"stage","start":76.211},{"w":"finds","start":76.611},{"w":"five","start":76.971},{"w":"words:","start":77.331},{"w":"the,","start":77.811},{"w":"dogs,","start":78.131},{"w":"were,","start":78.691},{"w":"barking,","start":79.011},{"w":"loudly.","start":79.651}]},{"id":"c12","start":80.691,"end":88.162,"marks":{},"text":"The morphological stage notices that \"dogs\" is \"dog\" plus a plural \"s\", and \"barking\" is \"bark\" plus \"i n g\".","words":[{"w":"The","start":80.691},{"w":"morphological","start":80.811},{"w":"stage","start":81.651},{"w":"notices","start":82.011},{"w":"that","start":82.611},{"w":"\"dogs\"","start":82.811},{"w":"is","start":83.251},{"w":"\"dog\"","start":83.451},{"w":"plus","start":83.811},{"w":"a","start":84.131},{"w":"plural","start":84.211},{"w":"\"s\",","start":84.851},{"w":"and","start":85.091},{"w":"\"barking\"","start":85.491},{"w":"is","start":86.091},{"w":"\"bark\"","start":86.331},{"w":"plus","start":86.771},{"w":"\"i","start":87.251},{"w":"n","start":87.631},{"w":"g\".","start":88.011}]},{"id":"c13","start":88.562,"end":93.973,"marks":{},"text":"The syntactic stage works out that \"dogs\" is the subject: they are the ones doing the barking.","words":[{"w":"The","start":88.562},{"w":"syntactic","start":88.682},{"w":"stage","start":89.362},{"w":"works","start":89.802},{"w":"out","start":90.122},{"w":"that","start":90.322},{"w":"\"dogs\"","start":90.562},{"w":"is","start":91.042},{"w":"the","start":91.242},{"w":"subject:","start":91.402},{"w":"they","start":92.122},{"w":"are","start":92.402},{"w":"the","start":92.562},{"w":"ones","start":92.682},{"w":"doing","start":93.002},{"w":"the","start":93.282},{"w":"barking.","start":93.442}]},{"id":"c14","start":94.373,"end":99.175,"marks":{},"text":"The semantic stage understands the meaning: some animals were making a loud noise.","words":[{"w":"The","start":94.373},{"w":"semantic","start":94.533},{"w":"stage","start":95.093},{"w":"understands","start":95.533},{"w":"the","start":96.173},{"w":"meaning:","start":96.373},{"w":"some","start":96.893},{"w":"animals","start":97.253},{"w":"were","start":97.773},{"w":"making","start":97.893},{"w":"a","start":98.213},{"w":"loud","start":98.373},{"w":"noise.","start":98.693}]},{"id":"c15","start":99.575,"end":107.126,"marks":{},"text":"And the pragmatic stage reads between the lines. If someone says this to you at home, they might mean: go and check who's at the door.","words":[{"w":"And","start":99.575},{"w":"the","start":99.655},{"w":"pragmatic","start":99.775},{"w":"stage","start":100.455},{"w":"reads","start":100.895},{"w":"between","start":101.295},{"w":"the","start":101.575},{"w":"lines.","start":101.735},{"w":"If","start":102.375},{"w":"someone","start":102.755},{"w":"says","start":103.135},{"w":"this","start":103.415},{"w":"to","start":103.615},{"w":"you","start":103.735},{"w":"at","start":103.935},{"w":"home,","start":104.135},{"w":"they","start":104.455},{"w":"might","start":104.655},{"w":"mean:","start":104.975},{"w":"go","start":105.415},{"w":"and","start":105.735},{"w":"check","start":105.975},{"w":"who's","start":106.255},{"w":"at","start":106.575},{"w":"the","start":106.695},{"w":"door.","start":106.815}]}],"title":"One sentence, five stages","shortTitle":"One sentence, five stages","props":{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"“The dogs were barking loudly”","columns":["Stage","What it finds"],"rows":[["Lexical","The · dogs · were · barking · loudly"],["Morphological","dog + s,  bark + ing"],["Syntactic","“dogs” is the subject"],["Semantic","animals making noise"],["Pragmatic","someone may be at the door"]],"highlight":[{"row":4}]},"start":68.433,"end":107.126,"startFrame":2053,"durationInFrames":1188},{"id":"ambiguity","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c16","start":108.033,"end":116.994,"marks":{},"text":"So why is this hard for a computer? One word explains most of it: ambiguity. Ambiguity is when the same words can be read in more than one way.","words":[{"w":"So","start":108.033},{"w":"why","start":108.193},{"w":"is","start":108.433},{"w":"this","start":108.633},{"w":"hard","start":108.833},{"w":"for","start":109.113},{"w":"a","start":109.273},{"w":"computer?","start":109.393},{"w":"One","start":110.033},{"w":"word","start":110.393},{"w":"explains","start":110.673},{"w":"most","start":111.353},{"w":"of","start":111.633},{"w":"it:","start":111.753},{"w":"ambiguity.","start":112.033},{"w":"Ambiguity","start":113.233},{"w":"is","start":114.193},{"w":"when","start":114.353},{"w":"the","start":114.553},{"w":"same","start":114.673},{"w":"words","start":114.953},{"w":"can","start":115.273},{"w":"be","start":115.393},{"w":"read","start":115.553},{"w":"in","start":115.793},{"w":"more","start":115.993},{"w":"than","start":116.193},{"w":"one","start":116.433},{"w":"way.","start":116.713}]},{"id":"c17","start":117.394,"end":119.662,"marks":{},"text":"Take this sentence: \"I saw her duck.\"","words":[{"w":"Take","start":117.394},{"w":"this","start":117.714},{"w":"sentence:","start":117.954},{"w":"\"I","start":118.554},{"w":"saw","start":118.834},{"w":"her","start":119.074},{"w":"duck.\"","start":119.274}]},{"id":"c18","start":120.062,"end":125.353,"marks":{},"text":"It's like an optical illusion. One picture, two images, and you can't see both at once.","words":[{"w":"It's","start":120.062},{"w":"like","start":120.262},{"w":"an","start":120.422},{"w":"optical","start":120.542},{"w":"illusion.","start":121.062},{"w":"One","start":121.902},{"w":"picture,","start":122.222},{"w":"two","start":122.862},{"w":"images,","start":123.182},{"w":"and","start":123.742},{"w":"you","start":123.862},{"w":"can't","start":124.022},{"w":"see","start":124.302},{"w":"both","start":124.502},{"w":"at","start":124.822},{"w":"once.","start":124.982}]}],"title":"Ambiguity","shortTitle":"Ambiguity","props":{"kicker":"Why it's hard","term":"Ambiguity","definition":"When the same words can be read in more than one way.","example":"I saw her duck.","analogy":"An optical illusion: one picture, two images."},"start":108.033,"end":125.353,"startFrame":3241,"durationInFrames":547},{"id":"duck","kind":"core","component":"Chat","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c19","start":126.267,"end":135.446,"marks":{},"text":"Here's how that plays out in a conversation. You type: \"I saw her duck.\" A careful assistant has to ask: do you mean her pet duck, or that she ducked down?","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":126.407},{"w":"how","start":126.547},{"w":"that","start":126.747},{"w":"plays","start":126.907},{"w":"out","start":127.267},{"w":"in","start":127.427},{"w":"a","start":127.547},{"w":"conversation.","start":127.627},{"w":"You","start":128.587},{"w":"type:","start":128.827},{"w":"\"I","start":129.387},{"w":"saw","start":129.627},{"w":"her","start":129.947},{"w":"duck.\"","start":130.187},{"w":"A","start":130.667},{"w":"careful","start":130.907},{"w":"assistant","start":131.387},{"w":"has","start":132.027},{"w":"to","start":132.187},{"w":"ask:","start":132.387},{"w":"do","start":132.787},{"w":"you","start":132.947},{"w":"mean","start":133.147},{"w":"her","start":133.307},{"w":"pet","start":133.467},{"w":"duck,","start":133.747},{"w":"or","start":134.107},{"w":"that","start":134.307},{"w":"she","start":134.507},{"w":"ducked","start":134.747},{"w":"down?","start":135.107}]}],"title":"Ambiguity in a chat","shortTitle":"“I saw her duck”: why computers get confused","props":{"title":"Same words, two meanings","messages":[{"role":"user","text":"I saw her duck."},{"role":"ai","text":"Do you mean her pet duck, or that she ducked down?"}]},"start":126.267,"end":135.446,"startFrame":3788,"durationInFrames":303},{"id":"levels","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c20","start":136.367,"end":140.796,"marks":{},"text":"Ambiguity hides at different stages. Here are the two you'll meet most often.","words":[{"w":"Ambiguity","start":136.367},{"w":"hides","start":137.167},{"w":"at","start":137.527},{"w":"different","start":137.727},{"w":"stages.","start":138.087},{"w":"Here","start":138.767},{"w":"are","start":139.167},{"w":"the","start":139.287},{"w":"two","start":139.407},{"w":"you'll","start":139.567},{"w":"meet","start":139.847},{"w":"most","start":140.087},{"w":"often.","start":140.327}]},{"id":"c21","start":141.196,"end":147.994,"marks":{},"text":"Lexical ambiguity is one word with two meanings, like \"bank\": the side of a river, or the place that keeps your money.","words":[{"w":"Lexical","start":141.196},{"w":"ambiguity","start":141.676},{"w":"is","start":142.396},{"w":"one","start":142.556},{"w":"word","start":142.836},{"w":"with","start":143.076},{"w":"two","start":143.276},{"w":"meanings,","start":143.516},{"w":"like","start":144.156},{"w":"\"bank\":","start":144.476},{"w":"the","start":144.876},{"w":"side","start":145.276},{"w":"of","start":145.676},{"w":"a","start":145.796},{"w":"river,","start":145.916},{"w":"or","start":146.356},{"w":"the","start":146.516},{"w":"place","start":146.716},{"w":"that","start":146.956},{"w":"keeps","start":147.156},{"w":"your","start":147.476},{"w":"money.","start":147.636}]},{"id":"c22","start":148.394,"end":158.895,"marks":{"verdict":156.114},"text":"Syntactic ambiguity is one sentence with two structures, like \"I saw the man with the telescope\". Who has the telescope? Each stage clears up its own kind of ambiguity.","words":[{"w":"Syntactic","start":148.394},{"w":"ambiguity","start":149.034},{"w":"is","start":149.754},{"w":"one","start":149.954},{"w":"sentence","start":150.194},{"w":"with","start":150.714},{"w":"two","start":150.914},{"w":"structures,","start":151.154},{"w":"like","start":151.914},{"w":"\"I","start":152.234},{"w":"saw","start":152.554},{"w":"the","start":152.794},{"w":"man","start":152.954},{"w":"with","start":153.234},{"w":"the","start":153.394},{"w":"telescope\".","start":153.514},{"w":"Who","start":154.474},{"w":"has","start":154.754},{"w":"the","start":154.954},{"w":"telescope?","start":155.154},{"w":"Each","start":156.114},{"w":"stage","start":156.474},{"w":"clears","start":156.834},{"w":"up","start":157.274},{"w":"its","start":157.434},{"w":"own","start":157.594},{"w":"kind","start":157.834},{"w":"of","start":157.994},{"w":"ambiguity.","start":158.074}]}],"title":"Ambiguity at each stage","shortTitle":"Ambiguity at each stage","props":{"kicker":"Two kinds","title":"Ambiguity hides at different stages","columns":[{"title":"Lexical","items":["one word, two meanings","“bank”: river or money?"],"tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Syntactic","items":["one sentence, two structures","“I saw the man with the telescope”"],"tone":"neutral"}],"verdict":{"text":"Each stage clears up its own kind of ambiguity","at":"c22@verdict"}},"start":136.367,"end":158.895,"startFrame":4091,"durationInFrames":703},{"id":"quiz","kind":"quiz","component":"Quiz","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c23","start":159.8,"end":164.605,"marks":{},"text":"Time for a quick quiz. Which stage decides that \"bank\" means the side of a river?","words":[{"w":"Time","start":159.8},{"w":"for","start":160.12},{"w":"a","start":160.4},{"w":"quick","start":160.68},{"w":"quiz.","start":160.96},{"w":"Which","start":161.24},{"w":"stage","start":161.6},{"w":"decides","start":162.04},{"w":"that","start":162.56},{"w":"\"bank\"","start":162.8},{"w":"means","start":163.2},{"w":"the","start":163.453},{"w":"side","start":163.707},{"w":"of","start":163.96},{"w":"a","start":164.08},{"w":"river?","start":164.2}]},{"id":"c24","start":165.005,"end":170.061,"marks":{},"text":"Pause the video and pick one. Lexica